<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nine Years' War (Ireland)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1593–1603</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Tyrone's Rebellion</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Nine Years' War was a rebellion of Gaelic Irish lords against English rule, fought from 1593 to 1603. Led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hugh-oneill-earl-of-tyrone">Hugh O'Neill, Earl of Tyrone</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-hugh-odonnell">Red Hugh O'Donnell</a>, with Maguire of Fermanagh and other Ulster lords, it won victories such as the Yellow Ford in 1598. A Spanish force landed at Kinsale in 1601, but defeat there led to O'Neill's surrender in 1603, the Flight of the Earls in 1607 and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/plantation-of-ulster">Plantation of Ulster</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nine-years-war-ireland.jpg" alt="Nine Years' War (Ireland)" width="320" height="417" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jacobfrid · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nine_Years_War_January1600.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
